---
import SourcePanel from '../components/SourcePanel.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { ASSETS } from '../data/assets';
import { SOURCES } from '../data/sources';

const title = 'Grave Seasons Collectibles - Crops, Tools, Items & Launch Tracker';
const description =
  'Pre-launch Grave Seasons collectibles guide framework for crops, tools, forage goods, crafted items, and special objects, using only official Steam and Blumhouse facts.';
const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Collectibles', url: '/collectibles/' },
];
const sources = [SOURCES.steam, SOURCES.blumhouse, SOURCES.blumhouseMedia];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} image={ASSETS.farmHarvest.src}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
    <p class="section-kicker">Collection framework</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-black leading-tight text-bone md:text-5xl">
      Grave Seasons Collectibles
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-fog">
      This page reserves the collectible and item-tracking URL before launch. Steam confirms farming, foraging, crafting, crops, a farm, mines, and multiple Ashenridge locations, but it does not publish a complete crop list, tool list, seed catalog, recipe list, or special-item checklist yet.
    </p>

    <figure class="mt-8">
      <img
        src={ASSETS.farmHarvest.src}
        alt={ASSETS.farmHarvest.alt}
        width={ASSETS.farmHarvest.width}
        height={ASSETS.farmHarvest.height}
        class="rounded-md border border-white/10"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-xs text-fog">{ASSETS.farmHarvest.credit}</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section class="prose-page mt-8">
      <h2>What is officially confirmed</h2>
      <p>
        Grave Seasons is presented as a farming and life sim with supernatural investigation layered on top. The official Steam page describes crop harvesting, foraging, crafting, one year of in-game pressure, seven major locations, and 70+ interiors. That is enough to build a launch tracker, but not enough to publish exact item names or drop rates.
      </p>
      <p>
        For SEO and user trust, this guide separates system categories from confirmed item data. Categories can exist before launch because official pages already describe farming, gathering, crafting, and exploration. Specific item rows should wait for direct in-game verification or a published official list.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <p class="section-kicker">Launch checklist</p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-black text-bone">Collectible data to verify after release</h2>
      <div class="mt-5 overflow-x-auto rounded-md border border-white/10">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[720px] border-collapse text-sm">
          <thead class="bg-moss/25 text-left text-bone">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-4 py-3">Category</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3">Pre-launch status</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3">Fields to verify</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-fog">
            <tr class="border-t border-white/10">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-bone">Crops and seeds</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Farming and crop harvesting are official; exact crop names are not published.</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Season, seed source, growth time, sale value, recipe use, and quest use.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-white/10">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-bone">Foraged goods</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Foraging is official; location tables need in-game verification.</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Location, season, respawn behavior, gift value, crafting use, and spoiler risk.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-white/10">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-bone">Tools and farm upgrades</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">The farm and farming loop are official; tool tiers are not listed yet.</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Unlock source, upgrade material, cost, stamina impact, and location requirement.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-white/10">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-bone">Crafted items</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Crafting is official; recipe names and ingredient counts are not published.</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Recipe source, ingredients, output, use case, sale value, and quest dependency.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-white/10">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-bone">Investigation objects</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">The murder mystery is official; clue names should remain spoiler-labeled.</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Trigger, location, victim link, killer-campaign variant, and spoiler-safe summary.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="prose-page mt-10">
      <h2>How this page should grow</h2>
      <p>
        After launch, this URL should become the inventory hub for players who want practical item answers without story spoilers. Crop and tool rows can stay spoiler-light, while investigation objects should use spoiler warnings because Steam confirms that the killer, targets, and campaign can change between playthroughs.
      </p>
      <p>
        The first release-day update should prioritize early farm tools, first-season crops, common forage items, and any object that blocks walkthrough progress. Romance gift data belongs primarily in the <a href="/romance-guide/">romance guide</a>, but this page can cross-link confirmed item uses once both pages have matching evidence.
      </p>
    </section>

    <SourcePanel sources={sources} />
  </article>
</Layout>
